+# Releases
+
+Releases happen when the team agrees the main branch is ready, which is usually every second week after the planning meeting. 
+
+## Before release
+
+Read the changelog from top to bottom and make sure that every entry describes the change in words a customer would understand. 
+
+## During release
+
+Bump the version in package.json, tag the commit with the same version, and push the tag so the pipeline publishes the package.
+
+## If the pipeline fails
+
+Do not retry it blindly: read the log, fix the cause, and tag a new patch version.
